---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Your music, in the notch</h1>
      <p class="lede">Warble shows what's playing in your Mac's notch. Hover over it to see the song, then play, pause, skip or switch speakers. When nothing's playing, it stays out of sight, and a hover brings back the last song so you can pick up where you left off.</p>
      <p class="meta">Free and open source, for macOS 15 or later. Warble is still being built, and the first beta isn't out yet.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="button big" href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble">Follow it on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="small">
    <div class="wrap narrow-text">
      <p>It works with Apple Music, Spotify, podcasts and video in your browser, and on Macs without a notch too. There's no account and nothing to set up, though <a href="/docs/settings/">Settings</a> lets you change the text size or what a hover shows. If something stops it seeing what's playing, it tells you how to <a href="/docs/when-nothing-shows/">fix it</a>. The <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md">roadmap</a> lists what's coming in each release.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px); }
  .hero .wrap { justify-items: start; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px); margin: 0; }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(19px, 2.2vw, 22px); margin: 0; max-width: 30em; }
  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; align-items: center; width: 100%; }
  .button.big { min-height: 52px; padding: 12px 22px; font-size: 18px; }
  .meta { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }

  section { padding-block: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
  .narrow-text p { max-width: 36em; }
  .small p { font-size: 19px; margin: 0; }
  .small a { font-weight: 700; }
</style>
